  'sy.note': 'The "real edge" is about the same for every system (Banker ≈1.06%). A system only changes the shape and the swings of your results.',
  'rx.lead': 'Baccarat tables show scoreboards called "roads". Here are the five that baccarat fans talk about, on a sample shoe.',
  'rx.bead': 'Bead Plate', 'rx.bead.d': 'Every result in order, top to bottom, then the next column. Red = Banker, blue = Player, green = Tie. The small dots in the corners are pairs.',
  'rx.big': 'Big Road', 'rx.big.d': 'Down while the same side keeps winning, a new column to the right when it changes. A tie is a green slash on the last circle. Past six rows it bends right — the "dragon tail".',
  'rx.eye': 'Big Eye Boy', 'rx.eye.d': 'Red when the Big Road\'s pattern repeats the column before, blue when it breaks it. Drawn as hollow circles.',
  'rx.small': 'Small Road', 'rx.small.d': 'The same idea, comparing two columns back. Drawn as filled dots.',
  'rx.roach': 'Cockroach Pig', 'rx.roach.d': 'Compares three columns back. Drawn as slashes — like a cockroach\'s tracks.',
  'rx.ask': 'Ask road', 'rx.ask.d': 'Which colours the three derived roads would get if the next coup were Banker (or Player).',
  'rx.warn': 'Roads are a tidy record of the past. Every coup is independent, so no road can predict the next winner. Enjoy them as part of the game.',
  'lsn.lead': 'Learn the drawing rules, the payouts, reading the roads and protecting your money with problems. Each lesson: a short explanation, then 5 problems — 4 right to pass.',
